<item>
            <title>[LU-20267] kernel update [RHEL 8.10 4.18.0-553.125.1.el8_10]</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20267</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Security Fix(es) for kernel 4.18.0-553.125.1.el8_10:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: &quot;Fragnesia&quot; is a variant of Dirty Frag vulnerability in the ESP/XFRM leading to Local Privilege Escalation (LPE) vulnerability in the Linux kernel (CVE-2026-46300)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: Read root-owned files as an unprivileged user (CVE-2026-46333)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:19666&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:19666&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Security Fix(es) for kernel 4.18.0-553.124.1.el8_10:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: &quot;Dirty Frag&quot; is a new universal Local Privilege Escalation (LPE) vulnerability in the Linux kernel (CVE-2026-43284)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://access.redhat.com/errata/product/479/ver=/rhel---8/x86_64/RHSA-2026:16195&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://access.redhat.com/errata/product/479/ver=/rhel---8/x86_64/RHSA-2026:16195&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
